Zero OS 0.9 actual network, native compiler and UI verification

From repository root, with a frozen ISO and its exact SHA256:
  python3 verification/network-0.9.0/run.py --iso build/zero.iso --sha HASH \
    --label UNIQUE_LABEL --guest-compilers --storage
Use a new label to preserve old evidence. --modes selects BIOS32, BIOS64,
UEFI32 and/or UEFI64. The default compute thread is 3; --compute-thread 2 is
only for older candidate reproducibility and skips the new numbering/pixel
checks. --public-host '' skips external DNS. The default public name
10.0.2.2.nip.io resolves to the local HTTP fixture, not an Internet HTTP peer.

The host Python files only orchestrate QEMU, keyboard, independent fixtures
and assertions. Guest implementation is the project's own Zero code.
The runner requires existing local QEMU/firmware/Pillow; it downloads nothing.
Actual PCnet frames are captured with filter-dump and decoded independently;
DHCP must finish before any input. BIOS guest memory snapshots are read-only.
No guest state is patched. Native1920x1080 screenshots are not resized.

Default runs attach no data disks. --storage copies only the existing private
ZeroFS/ext4 verification fixtures and attaches those copies. It never attaches
build/data.img or build/data.vdi. All private disk and ISO hashes must remain
unchanged after VM shutdown. Pflash variables are also private copies.

Current matrix verifies task numbering/pause behavior, one-based pixel corners
and rejection bounds, automatic link recovery while computation actually stops,
local HTTP, public DNS, production WiFi modal PS/2 handling and restoration.
--guest-compilers tests default native Zero/Ezero commands, meaningful errors,
u64, EOF, output cap and recovery. --storage adds one-based disk labels and
absolute/relative ext4 read regression. See run.py for exact oracles.

Stock QEMU has no native WiFi radio. The actual VM tests the production
no-adapter modal; hosted simulated radio screens are separate evidence.
Native VirtualBox/physical hardware and public HTTP remain outside this proof.
A separate host-only example.com:80 probe records external egress availability.

Per-mode JSON/text/serial logs and native PNGs are reviewable evidence. Private
pflash variables, raw memory, PPMs, disk copies and PCAP are internal artifacts.
Results apply only after completed runs against the recorded exact ISO hash.
Current final result: final-880feb36/results.txt and matrix.json.
